      "sourceCount": 1,
      "datePrecision": "month",
      "dateRaw": "2025-12",
      "summary": "CVE-2025-66414, **CVSS 8.1**. An unauthenticated HTTP MCP server running on localhost without `enableDnsRebindingProtection` can be made to invoke tools by a malicious website via DNS rebinding that bypasses the same-origin policy. **Fixed in v1.24.0**: `createMcpExpressApp()` now enables protection by default when binding to localhost",
