      "regions": ["GLOBAL"],
      "landmark": false,
      "disputed": false,
      "sourceCount": 2,
      "datePrecision": "day",
      "dateRaw": "2025-12-29",
      "summary": "Zenity Labs: the feature (launched at Build 2025) lets agents share capabilities, and **once enabled it exposes one agent's knowledge, tools and topics to every other agent in the same environment** — and **① it is on by default for all new agents, ② no interface shows who has connected to your agent**. Attackers can use this to impersonate an organization and trigger sensitive operations unnoticed. Zenity's conclusion: \"**Always assume that any agent with connected agents enabled is anonymously reachable from the entire internet**\"",
